<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Damghan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Damghan is a city in Semnan province, northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, on the old road from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tehran">Tehran</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khorasan">Khorasan</a>. It holds the Tarikhaneh, one of the oldest surviving mosques in Iran. In 1729 Nader, the future <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah</a>, defeated the Afghan ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashraf-hotak">Ashraf Hotak</a> near the city, beginning the expulsion of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghans">Afghans</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/damghan.jpg" alt="Damghan" width="320" height="246" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: حسن اثباتی لواسانی · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Damghan-1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
